client: a MOTD that is a web page is not drawn as text

The client already skipped a MOTD beginning <!DOCTYPE HTML>. Servers of the
2010s sent a one-line <meta http-equiv="Refresh"> instead, to bounce the old
VGUI MOTD window to their website; drawn as text that is a yellow bar of tag
soup over the game, in a recording or a live join alike. Any HTML tag is a
web page now, and a web page is not shown.

--- a/cl_dll/hud/MOTD.cpp
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/MOTD.cpp
@@ -146,7 +146,11 @@
 	strcat( m_szMOTD, reader.ReadString() );
 
 	// we still don't support html tags in motd :(
-	if( strcasestr( m_szMOTD, "<!DOCTYPE HTML>" ) )
+	// A web page is a web page whether or not it begins with a doctype: servers of the
+	// 2010s sent a one-line <meta http-equiv="Refresh"> to bounce the MOTD window to
+	// their site, and drawn as text that is a yellow bar of tag soup over the game.
+	if( strcasestr( m_szMOTD, "<!DOCTYPE HTML>" ) || strcasestr( m_szMOTD, "<html" ) || strcasestr( m_szMOTD, "<meta" )
+		|| strcasestr( m_szMOTD, "<body" ) || strcasestr( m_szMOTD, "http-equiv" ) )
 	{
 		Reset();
 		ignoreThisMotd = true;
